CAT = "rotxLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Under Law 38/2003, who may carry passengers for payment in a taxi?",
 "Only an authorised carrier", ["Any driver with a B licence", "Any member of a taxi union", "Any car owner who registers"],
 "Law 38/2003 allows taxi and rental transport only by authorised carriers (transportatori autorizați) holding a valid taxi authorisation or certified copy for each vehicle."),
("Taxi transport in a Romanian town is organised as a public service by:",
 "The local authorities", ["The Romanian Road Authority", "The Ministry of Finance", "The national taxi chamber"],
 "Taxi services are community public utility services organised and coordinated by the local council and town hall of each administrative area (Law 38/2003, art. 2 and 3)."),
("Which body authorises carriers for transport in rental mode (închiriere)?",
 "The Romanian Road Authority", ["The town hall's taxi office", "The traffic police", "The consumer protection office"],
 "For taxi transport the authorising authority is the town hall's transport service; for rental transport with a driver it is the Romanian Road Authority (ARR)."),
("A carrier's taxi authorisation (autorizație taxi) is issued:",
 "For one specific vehicle", ["For the driver, in any car", "For a whole fleet at once", "For one specific route"],
 "The taxi authorisation is a certified copy of the carrier's transport authorisation, issued per vehicle and showing its registration number."),
("Can a taxi authorisation be moved to another car or another carrier?",
 "No, it is non-transferable", ["Yes, with the driver's consent", "Yes, within the same county", "Yes, for up to 30 days"],
 "The law makes the taxi authorisation unique and non-transferable from one carrier to another and from one vehicle to another. Replacing a car needs a new copy from the authority."),
("A self-employed carrier (persoană fizică autorizată) may run taxi transport with:",
 "A single vehicle", ["Up to three vehicles", "Up to five vehicles", "Any number of vehicles"],
 "Law 38/2003 limits an authorised individual carrier to one vehicle, owned or leased by them or their spouse."),
("A family association may use as many taxis as:",
 "Members holding an attestation", ["Members of the family, any age", "Cars it owns or leases", "Licences the town hall sets"],
 "The number of vehicles a family association may use is at most the number of its members who drive the taxi and hold a professional attestation."),
("Which paper must always be on board a working taxi together with its badges?",
 "The taxi authorisation", ["The carrier's bank statement", "The driver's employment contract", "The town's taxi regulation"],
 "The taxi authorisation (or the certified copy for rental transport) must be on board and is valid only together with the two badges (ecusoane) and the documents listed in art. 12."),
("Which driver document is part of the papers a passenger taxi must carry?",
 "The professional attestation", ["The driving school diploma", "The full birth certificate", "A recent criminal record extract"],
 "Art. 12 lists the driver's professional attestation certificate among the documents that must be on board when carrying passengers."),
("A taxi must carry a copy of the bulletin that shows the taximeter has passed its:",
 "Metrological check", ["Exhaust emissions test", "Fire extinguisher check", "Annual road tax review"],
 "The documents on board include a copy of the metrological verification bulletin for the taximeter, issued after a check by the Romanian Bureau of Legal Metrology."),
("A taxi linked to a dispatch centre must carry a copy of:",
 "The dispatch contract", ["The dispatcher's tax return", "A list of each day's bookings", "The radio's purchase invoice"],
 "When a taxi is assigned to a taxi dispatcher (dispecerat), a copy of the dispatch contract is among the documents that must be on board."),
("Which insurance must a passenger taxi carry, besides compulsory motor liability (RCA)?",
 "Passengers and their belongings", ["The driver's own home and contents", "The carrier's own life cover", "Damage to the meter only"],
 "Law 38/2003 requires insurance for the persons carried, their belongings and goods, for risks that fall on the carrier, in addition to RCA."),
("At a check, a taxi is missing one of its required documents. What happens first?",
 "The authorisation is held back", ["The car is taken off the road", "Only a verbal warning is given", "The driver's licence is cancelled"],
 "The inspector withholds the taxi authorisation until the carrier proves the document exists and is valid. If that is not proven within 30 days, the authorisation is withdrawn."),
("If the missing document is still not produced within 30 days, the taxi authorisation is:",
 "Withdrawn with its badges", ["Extended for 30 more days", "Moved to the driver's name", "Kept, with a note on file"],
 "Art. 12 says the authorisation and its badges are withdrawn, and the authority can then assign it to another carrier."),
("Which certificate does the Romanian Auto Register (RAR) issue for a car used as a taxi?",
 "The approval certificate", ["The professional attestation", "The tariff approval notice", "The type approval of the meter"],
 "Only cars approved by RAR may be used as taxis. RAR issues the certificate of approval (certificat de agreare), endorsed at the periodic technical inspection."),
("In the traffic flow, who must take part when town hall or consumer inspectors stop a taxi for a check?",
 "The traffic police", ["The dispatcher", "The carrier's manager", "A court bailiff"],
 "Several authorities may check taxis, but in moving traffic most of them may stop a vehicle only together with the traffic police (Law 38/2003, art. 37)."),
("During a ride with the meter on Ocupat, a check is normally carried out only:",
 "In a flagrant case", ["Every ten kilometres driven", "At the client's own request", "Once the fare passes a set sum"],
 "The law says checks while the taxi is engaged on a ride are made, as a rule, only in flagrant cases, so passengers are not delayed."),
("Which authority checks that taxi meters measure correctly while in use?",
 "The metrology bureau (BRML)", ["The Romanian Road Authority", "The local council tax office", "The territorial labour inspectorate"],
 "Taximeters in use are under legal metrological control by the Romanian Bureau of Legal Metrology (BRML), which carries out the first check after installation and later periodic checks."),
("In a Romanian town, who issues the authorisation for taxi transport?",
 "The town hall's transport office", ["The Romanian Road Authority", "The county prefect's office", "The national taxi chamber"],
 "For taxi transport the authorising authority is the transport department of the town hall (or Bucharest City Hall), licensed for this by ANRSC. ARR authorises rental transport with driver."),
("A taxi carrier that is a company must appoint a person who runs its taxi work day to day, called:",
 "A transport manager", ["A chief dispatcher", "A fleet maintenance chief", "A taxi union delegate"],
 "Companies and family associations must have a transport manager for taxi and rental transport, holding an ARR certificate of professional competence."),
("A transport manager for taxi and rental transport may manage the work of:",
 "One carrier only", ["Up to three carriers", "Any number of carriers", "All carriers in one county"],
 "Law 38/2003 says one taxi and rental transport manager may run the activity of a single authorised carrier."),
("Under Law 38/2003, what comes first in every taxi and rental activity?",
 "Life and the environment", ["The carrier's profit", "The speed of each ride", "The dispatcher's orders on duty"],
 "Art. 2 states that in all relations arising from taxi and rental transport, protecting human life and the environment has priority."),
("Who sets the maximum distance tariffs for passenger taxis in a town?",
 "The local council", ["Each taxi driver", "The Romanian Road Authority", "The dispatch company"],
 "The local council (in Bucharest, the General Council) sets the maximum distance tariffs by decision, using the national methodology. Tariffs vary by municipality."),
("A taxi authorisation is valid only when it is shown together with its:",
 "Two badges (ecusoane)", ["The fuel receipts", "Client feedback forms", "The driver's CV"],
 "Each taxi authorisation is issued with two badges carrying the same validity, and the authorisation is valid only in their presence."),
("Who decides local taxi rules such as compulsory working hours and 24-hour cover?",
 "The local council", ["The individual driver", "The national police", "The car manufacturer"],
 "Local authorities issue the town's taxi regulation, including compulsory work schedules, round-the-clock service and restrictions. Rules vary by municipality."),
("Carrying passengers for payment in a car with no valid taxi authorisation or certified copy is:",
 "Forbidden", ["Allowed for short trips", "Allowed at night only", "Allowed with a receipt"],
 "Art. 7 forbids public transport of persons for payment in a car without, as the case may be, a valid taxi authorisation or certified copy."),
("Which body may a client write to about a taxi driver's bad practice, besides the town hall?",
 "The consumer protection office", ["The county tax office", "The Romanian Road Authority", "The territorial labour inspectorate"],
 "Clients may report poor practice to the town hall of the authorising locality and to the county office of the National Authority for Consumer Protection (ANPC)."),
("Placing taxi signs or a roof light on a car with no taxi authorisation is:",
 "Forbidden", ["Allowed when parked", "Allowed for training", "Allowed with a dispatcher"],
 "Art. 36 forbids fitting taxi or rental signs, markings, equipment or accessories to a vehicle that has no taxi authorisation or certified copy."),
]
